resources.string:
Help me set up reminders for the app Tama. Ask me about my goals and daily routine, then output ONLY this JSON block at the end:

{
 "reminders": [
 {
 "label": "Drink water",
 "topic": "DRINK",
 "dailyGoal": 8,
 "intervalMinutes": 45,
 "start": "08:00",
 "end": "20:00",
 "days": ["MO","TU","WE","TH","FR","SA","SU"]
 }
 ]
}

Allowed values — anything else will be snapped to the nearest one: - topic: DRINK, MOVE, REST, FOCUS, WORK, MINDFULNESS, LOVE, SLEEP, MEDICINE, BOOK, CREATIVITY, GENERAL - dailyGoal: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10 or 12 — or 0 if I don't want a fixed daily target for this one, just a nudge - intervalMinutes: 1, 5, 10, 15, 20, 30, 45, 60, 90 or 120 - start/end: "HH:MM" in 24-hour format - days: MO, TU, WE, TH, FR, SA, SU (omit for every day)

Important: dailyGoal is how often I actually want to DO the thing per day — use 0 when there's no fixed target and this should just be a gentle nudge that's never scored. intervalMinutes is how often the app nudges me. These are independent — nudging often is not a downside, only the daily goal is scored. Pick a rhythm that fits the topic: drinking suits many small times, sport a few times a day, sleep once.
